      "writtenOn": "2023-07-04T14:10:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What if the user of vmbase wants to extend what happens on a particular exception, eg. custom IRQ handling?\n\nI didn\u0027t move all the exception handling, only `sync_exception_current` is moved to vmbase as the translation/permission fault handling is tied to MemoryTracker and required by a normal flow.\nAn alternative to keep the extensibility is to duplicate this code in rialto.\n\n\u003e Why not extract the MemoryTracker functionality into helpers but leave the exception callbacks in place?\n\nWhat do you mean by extracting the MemoryTracker functionality into helpers? Can you detail this approach a bit?",
      "parentUuid": "99718f73_9c2d7fb2",
      "revId": "a07f55020fe2c6a7ce26a078f97a0c2d66a94dc4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "525475d0_f789c535",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-04T14:26:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`sync_exception_current` is what\u0027s called when the CPU triggers an exception. That can happen for many different reasons, only some of which are relevant to page table management - see here: https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0595/2020-12/AArch64-Registers/ESR-EL1--Exception-Syndrome-Register--EL1-\n\nThis particular implementation handles `DataAbortTranslationFault` and `DataAbortPermissionFault`, and will panic with a generic error message for all the other kinds of exceptions that exist.\n\nBy moving the entrypoint of the exception to `vmbase`, you are preventing users of that library from handling the other kinds of exceptions. Overriding can be useful for many reasons. For example, they might want to write a custom panic handler that provides extra information about certain types of errors. Or they might want to support a debugger that triggers an exception after every instruction.\n\nI would only move `handle_translation_fault` and `handle_permission_fault` (with their dependencies), and leave `sync_exception_current`, `handling_uart_exception` and `handle_exception` inside each client. It\u0027s absolutely fine to have some duplication there.",
      "parentUuid": "0aa88a5c_f967cd49",
      "revId": "a07f55020fe2c6a7ce26a078f97a0c2d66a94dc4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
