      "writtenOn": "2023-07-04T14:32:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re-reading your answer and maybe one thing that may not be clear - `sync_exception_current` is a handler for all **synchronous exceptions from EL1 caught by EL1** (\"current\"). There are other entry points for asynchronous exceptions, exceptions from lower levels (EL0) and combination thereof. \n\nYou seem to suggest that moving `sync_exception_current` still leaves the client with the other entry points. That\u0027s true, but they might want to handle more than just the two types of same-level synchronous exceptions that pvmfw currently handles.",
      "parentUuid": "525475d0_f789c535",
